### planning health
GET http://localhost:8085/actuator/health
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-health

### planning liveness
GET http://localhost:8085/actuator/health/liveness

### planning prometheus
GET http://localhost:8085/actuator/prometheus

### ---- P13 (ADR-0019): budgets, liabilities and what-if scenarios. Every route needs a USER token: sign in via
### identity.http (POST /v1/auth/login) and paste the accessToken below. Paste the ids the creates return.
@token = PASTE_AN_ACCESS_TOKEN
@budgetId = PASTE_A_BUDGET_ID
@liabilityId = PASTE_A_LIABILITY_ID
@scenarioId = PASTE_A_SCENARIO_ID

### budget: a monthly Rs 2,000 cap on food.dining and everything under it (thresholds default to 50/80/100 %)
POST http://localhost:8085/v1/budgets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: 11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-budget-create

{"name": "Eating out", "period": "monthly", "categoryPath": "food.dining", "limitPaise": 200000,
 "startsOn": "2026-10-01", "alertThresholds": [50, 80, 100]}

### budget: a weekly cap on all spend (no categoryPath), repeating every 7 days from startsOn
POST http://localhost:8085/v1/budgets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: 22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-budget-weekly

{"name": "This week", "period": "weekly", "limitPaise": 500000, "startsOn": "2026-10-26"}

### budgets: newest first, keyset paged (no OFFSET anywhere)
GET http://localhost:8085/v1/budgets?limit=25
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-budgets

### budgets: where every active budget stands in its current period (what p13-planning.html draws as bars).
### spentPaise comes from the ledger over Kafka - planning never takes spend from an API call.
GET http://localhost:8085/v1/budgets/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-status

### budget: one, with its ETag = version (If-Match for the patch below)
GET http://localhost:8085/v1/budgets/{{budgetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-budget

### budget: every period it has had, newest first
GET http://localhost:8085/v1/budgets/{{budgetId}}/history?limit=12
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-budget-history

### budget: raise the limit (name, limitPaise, rollover, alertThresholds, endsOn and status are patchable;
### period, categoryPath and startsOn are not - they decide what the stored periods mean)
PATCH http://localhost:8085/v1/budgets/{{budgetId}}
Content-Type: application/merge-patch+json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: "0"
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-budget-patch

{"limitPaise": 300000}

### budget: pause it - a paused budget is not tracking, so spend during the pause is not counted when it resumes
PATCH http://localhost:8085/v1/budgets/{{budgetId}}
Content-Type: application/merge-patch+json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: "1"
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-budget-pause

{"status": "paused"}

### budget: end it - the periods and alerts stay for the history, and it is read-only afterwards (409)
DELETE http://localhost:8085/v1/budgets/{{budgetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-budget-end

### liability: Rs 1,00,000 at 12 % over 12 months -> 888488 paise a month on the shared EMI engine
### (libs/portfolio-calc, A-74 - the same maths behind POST /v1/calc/emi). A loan carries no GST.
POST http://localhost:8085/v1/liabilities
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: 33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-liability-create

{"kind": "loan", "lender": "HDFC Bank", "principalPaise": 10000000, "aprBps": 1200, "tenureMonths": 12,
 "startDate": "2026-11-01"}

### liabilities: newest first, keyset paged
GET http://localhost:8085/v1/liabilities?limit=25
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-liabilities

### liability: the schedule written when it was recorded, never re-rated (a rate change is a new liability)
GET http://localhost:8085/v1/liabilities/{{liabilityId}}/schedule?limit=24
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-liability-schedule

### liability: rename the lender (only lender and status are patchable)
PATCH http://localhost:8085/v1/liabilities/{{liabilityId}}
Content-Type: application/merge-patch+json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: "0"
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-liability-patch

{"lender": "HDFC Bank Ltd"}

### liability: close it (publishes planning.liability.changed; it stays readable as closed)
DELETE http://localhost:8085/v1/liabilities/{{liabilityId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-liability-close

### scenario: save a copy of the account as it is now - active budgets, active liabilities and an assumed income.
### Evaluating it later applies the adjustments to this copy, so the answer does not drift with the account.
POST http://localhost:8085/v1/scenarios
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: 44444444-4444-4444-8444-444444444444
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-scenario-create

{"name": "Can I take a car loan?", "monthlyIncomePaise": 10000000, "adjustments": []}

### scenario: add a hypothetical Rs 5,00,000 car loan at 10 % over 60 months (10623.52 a month, same engine).
### The four kinds are setMonthlyIncome, setBudgetLimit, addLiability and removeLiability; one the snapshot
### cannot satisfy is refused with 422 SCENARIO_ADJUSTMENT_INVALID rather than ignored.
PATCH http://localhost:8085/v1/scenarios/{{scenarioId}}
Content-Type: application/merge-patch+json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: "0"
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-scenario-patch

{"adjustments": [{"kind": "addLiability", "lender": "Car loan", "principalPaise": 50000000, "aprBps": 1000,
                  "tenureMonths": 60}]}

### scenario: evaluate it - income against the adjusted outgo, line by line, and whether it fits
POST http://localhost:8085/v1/scenarios/{{scenarioId}}:evaluate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-scenario-evaluate

### scenarios: newest first, keyset paged
GET http://localhost:8085/v1/scenarios?limit=25
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-planning-scenarios
